; expect 42
; `docs/reference.md:808` promises that a `type` alias "does not create
; a new type - `StringList` and `[String]` are interchangeable". The
; compiler answered two different ways depending on POSITION: an alias
; was nominal where an argument is checked and transparent where a
; declared return is, so `(h 42)` was `AX3004: expected Count, found
; Int` while `(h (mkc 42))` ran and printed 42. `tcAliases` was filled
; at collection and read by `axiom symbols` and by nothing else.
;
; Three terms, and the third is the one with a wrong answer behind it:
;
;   a  an alias in ARGUMENT position, which used to be the refusal;
;   b  an alias reached through another alias, so expansion has to
;      re-enter rather than substitute once;
;   c  an alias to `Float`. This is why expanding in the checker alone
;      would have been a swapped defect rather than a fix:
;      `parseSigDecl` reconstructs one float flag per arrow position
;      FROM THE TOKENS, because float-ness is not observable at
;      runtime, and codegen reads those flags to decide `fmul` against
;      `mul`. A checker that says `Float` over an emitter that still
;      says `Int` computes `0.00` at exit 0 - measured, by ablating
;      the flag rewrite and running this file.
;
; `area` takes TWO parameters and multiplies them, with no float
; LITERAL anywhere in the body, because a literal operand decides
; float-ness on its own and would make this term pass either way.
(import Fmt)

(type Count = Int)

(type Tally = Count)

(type Real = Float)

(:: h (-> Count Int))

(fn (h c) c)

(:: mkc (-> Int Count))

(fn (mkc n) n)

(:: t (-> Tally Int))

(fn (t v) v)

(:: area (-> Real Real Real))

(fn (area w h) (* w h))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (if (&& (&& (== (h 20) 20) (== (h (mkc 1)) 1)) (&& (== (t 17) 17) (== (__floatToInt (area 3.0 1.5)) 4)))
    42
    1
  )
)
